  "status": "published",
  "title": "Edison Pendant Lamp",
  "summary": "A plug-in swag pendant on cloth cord with an exposed LED filament bulb. Wire a socket safely, once and properly.",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "estimatedHours": 2,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Work with nothing plugged in. Cut the cord to length, then strip 3/8 in of insulation off each conductor at the socket end with the wire stripper.",
    "Feed the cord through the socket cap and cord grip, tie an underwriter's knot so a tug on the cord pulls on the knot and not the screws.",
    "Find the neutral conductor (ribbed or marked) and wrap it clockwise round the silver screw; wrap the smooth hot conductor round the brass screw. Tighten both and check no strands stick out.",
    "Snap the socket shell over the interior and into the cap, and tighten the cord grip.",
    "Fit the polarized plug and the inline switch at the other end following their printed instructions, keeping the neutral on the wide blade.",
    "With the multimeter on continuity, confirm the wide plug blade connects to the socket's threaded shell and the narrow blade to the centre contact only with the switch on, and that the two never connect to each other.",
    "Drill a pilot hole into a ceiling joist, screw in the swag hook, drape the cord, fit the bulb and plug it in."
  ],
